---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Patient information and scan preparation"
  description="Prepare for your ultrasound appointment in Hobsonville. Learn what to bring, scan preparation, support-person guidance, results and payment information."
>
  <PageIntro
    title="Feel prepared for your visit."
    eyebrow="Patient information"
    description="A few practical details to help you arrive feeling comfortable and ready for your ultrasound."
  />
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container two-column">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Before your appointment</h2>
        <p>
          A referral is required for diagnostic scans. Bring your completed
          referral if it has not already been sent to us, along with any
          relevant previous imaging or reports.
        </p>
        <p>
          Preparation varies by examination. Please read your appointment
          instructions and the preparation on your scan’s service page.
        </p>
        <h3>Abdominal scans</h3>
        <p>
          No food or drink for 6 hours before your appointment, except plain
          water. Take prescribed medication as normal. If you have diabetes,
          check preparation with your doctor.
        </p>
        <h3>Pelvic and renal tract scans</h3>
        <p>
          A full bladder is required. Empty your bladder 1 hour before the scan
          and drink 3–4 glasses (approximately 800 mL) of water. If it is not
          full 10 minutes before the appointment, drink more. If it becomes
          uncomfortably full, you may release a small amount.
        </p>
        <h3>Combined abdomen and pelvis</h3>
        <p>
          Follow both the abdominal fasting instructions and the full-bladder
          instructions above. Plain water is permitted.
        </p>
        <h3>Pregnancy scans</h3>
        <p>
          For dating scans before 10 weeks, follow the full-bladder instructions
          above. Other obstetric examinations have no special preparation
          listed; follow the individual instructions provided with your
          appointment.
        </p>
        <h3>Musculoskeletal and vascular scans</h3>
        <p>
          No special preparation is listed. Wear clothing that allows access to
          the area being examined. A loose top or singlet is helpful for a
          shoulder scan; shorts or loose trousers for a knee scan.
        </p>
        <div class="notice">
          <p>
            If you have diabetes, difficulty with preparation, or questions
            about your instructions, contact your doctor or our reception team
            before your visit.
          </p>
        </div>
        <h2>At the clinic</h2>
        <p>
          Find us on Level 1 of the Hobson Centre, above Unichem Pharmacy at
          Woolworths, 124 Hobsonville Road. Free visitor parking is available.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may bring one adult support person. Please avoid bringing children
          where possible. If unavoidable, one child may attend with another
          responsible adult to supervise them.
        </p>
        <h2>After your scan</h2>
        <p>
          For diagnostic examinations, the images are reviewed by the reporting
          radiologist and your report is sent to your referring clinician when
          complete. Your referrer can explain the findings and discuss next
          steps.
        </p>
        <p>
          Images may be shared using a secure email link for $10 per study where
          not already included. Email reception for report requests.
        </p>
        <h2>Payment and appointment changes</h2>
        <p>
          Payment is due at your appointment. Please give at least 24 hours’
          notice if you need to cancel or reschedule. Late cancellation or
          non-attendance may incur a $50 fee.
        </p>
        <a href="/appointment-policy/">Read the full appointment policy</a>
      </div>
      <aside>
        <div class="sidebar-panel">
          <h2>Find your scan</h2>
          <p>
            Your examination page brings together preparation, pricing and
            booking information.
          </p>
          <a class="button" href="/services/">
            Explore examinations ↗
          </a>
          <p style="margin-top:1.5rem">
            <a href="/pricing/">Pricing and eligibility</a>
          </p>
          <p>
            <a href="/faq/">Frequently asked questions</a>
          </p>
          <a href="/contact/">Location and contact details</a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Callout />
</Layout>
